## Summary

I shipped a production-complete, native Apple (SwiftUI) parity of `features/admin/components/AlertDetailTimeline.tsx` as **8 files** in `apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/` (committed `8a5ce9ee1`, 1,724 insertions):

| File | Role |
|---|---|
| `AlertDetailTimeline.swift` | Main view: glass panel, header, phase switch, telemetry lifecycle |
| `.Adapter.swift` | Pure core: kind parsing, actor-aware/anonymous titles, icon/timestamp/a11y |
| `.Model.swift` | P1/S8 state-holder seam, projection, P1/S11 telemetry, P1/S10 i18n facade |
| `.Views.swift` | Timeline rail (kind-tinted dot + connector), freshness chip, banner, loading/error/empty |
| `.Previews.swift` | 6 state previews |
| `.Tests.swift` + `.ModelTests.swift` | 44 unit tests |
| `.strings` | i18n catalog (all source keys + native chrome) |

**Parity:** every web state reproduced (timeline/empty) plus the required P4 leaf states (loading/error/stale/offline + one-shot stale auto-refresh); exact semantic color mapping (created→accent, acknowledged→success, reopened→warning, commented→power-purple); SF-Symbol icon mapping; full VoiceOver/Dynamic Type; no HTTP in the view.

**In-scope verification — all green:**
- swiftformat `--lint`, swiftlint `--strict`, placeholder gate: **0 issues** across all files
- Island typecheck against the **real** design tokens + shared-component signatures: **passed** (caught & fixed a real `Date.FormatStyle` timezone-API bug)
- `swift test`: **44 tests, 0 failures**
- Full app build: **zero** errors in any AlertDetailTimeline file

